{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VBoNQ4beeBeEBws1YPEghM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '完全reframe为\"Do Reasoning LLMs Need Recovery-Aware Pruning?\"——controlled\n2\t  empirical study， 核心发现是surprising negative result：CKA functional overlap不预测RLVR recoverability，\n3\t  但α-scaled importance scoring确实优于vanilla magnitude pruning（与CKA理论联系薄弱）， SFT recovery对所有pruning方法都surprisingly\n4\t  effective。 GRPO未能逆转Standard在SFT阶段建立的优势，RASP在GRPO下无额外增益甚至略劣。 论文价值在于：(1)实验thoroughness本身（5-seed,\n5\t  3 sparsity, 4 methods, 2 recovery paradigms）， (2)α scoring作为简单有效的pruning改进的positive\n6\t  takeaway， (3)对recovery-aware pruning直觉假设的empirically grounded challenge。\n7\t\n8\t  '\n9\timagined_experiments:\n10\t- name: Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (Post-Prune)\n11\t  plan_id: plan_001\n12\t  description: Dense baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20 在完整1319样本上的post-prune评估\n13\t  expected_results:\n14\t    dense_baseline_gsm8k_1319: 0.764\n15\t    dense_baseline_ci95: ±0.023\n16\t    rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.293\n17\t    rasp_20_ci95: ±0.025\n18\t    standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.281\n19\t    standard_20_ci95: ±0.025\n20\t    rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 1.2\n21\t    gap_p_value_bootstrap: 0.34\n22\t    n_samples: 1319\n23\t  result_rationale: 'N=100时观测到31% vs 27%（4pp gap），但bootstrap CI为±9pp。 扩展到N=1319后CI缩至±2.5pp，真实gap收缩到~1.2pp，\n24\t    因为N=100的4pp gap本身就在seed方差范围内（reeval_postprune_definitive已显示）。 RASP的CKA加权在20% sparsity下只重排了少量边界MLP\n25\t    groups， 大部分pruning决策与Standard一致（两者共享~85%的pruned set）， 导致full eval下gap不显著。\n26\t\n27\t    '\n28\t  tables:\n29\t  - name: 'Table 1: Post-Prune GSM8K Accuracy (N=1319)'\n30\t    columns:\n31\t    - Model\n32\t    - Accuracy\n33\t    - 95% CI\n34\t    - vs Dense Drop\n35\t    rows:\n36\t    - - Dense Baseline\n37\t      - 76.4%\n38\t      - ±2.3pp\n39\t      - —\n40\t    - - RASP-20\n41\t      - 29.3%\n42\t      - ±2.5pp\n43\t      - -47.1pp\n44\t    - - Standard-20\n45\t      - 28.1%\n46\t      - ±2.5pp\n47\t      - -48.3pp\n48\t    - - Δ (RASP − Standard)\n49\t      - +1.2pp\n50\t      - ''\n51\t      - p=0.34\n52\t  figures_description:\n53\t  - 'Bar chart: 三个模型的GSM8K accuracy with error bars，视觉上RASP和Standard几乎无法区分'\n54\t  analysis: '核心发现：原始29% vs 1%的29x优势不可复现（已在reeval_postprune_definitive确认）， full eval进一步确认gap仅~1pp且不显著。\n55\t    这直接摧毁了Claim 1的基础——RASP并未在post-prune阶段提供qualitatively different的保留。 两种pruning方法都将模型从76%打到~29%，损失相似。\n56\t    论文中需reframe为：在moderate sparsity下，CKA-aware reranking对post-prune accuracy影响有限。\n57\t\n58\t    '\n59\t- name: SFT Warmup Recovery\n60\t  plan_id: plan_002\n61\t  description: SFT teacher-forcing恢复RASP_20和Standard_20的基本生成能力\n62\t  expected_results:\n63\t    sft_rasp_20_gsm8k_100: 0.57\n64\t    sft_standard_20_gsm8k_100: 0.64\n65\t    sft_gap_pp: -7\n66\t    sft_rasp_train_loss_final: 0.64\n67\t    sft_standard_train_loss_final: 0.64\n68\t    sft_rasp_token_accuracy: 0.83\n69\t    sft_standard_token_accuracy: 0.83\n70\t    eos_rate_both: 0.99\n71\t    total_steps: 1870\n72\t  result_rationale: '已完成实验（DONE）。Standard在SFT后反超RASP 7pp（64% vs 57%）。 这在worst档下的解释：RASP保护了functionally\n73\t    unique但SFT-unfriendly的structures， 而Standard保留了对teacher-forcing更responsive的structures。\n74\t    两者train loss和token accuracy完全相同（0.64, 83%）， 说明差异不在optimization landscape而在pruned\n75\t    model的representational capacity分配上。 关键是：SFT recovery本身extremely effective——从29%→57%/64%，恢复了大部分能力。\n76\t\n77\t    '\n78\t  tables:\n79\t  - name: 'Table 2: SFT Recovery Results'\n80\t    columns:\n81\t    - Pruned Model\n82\t    - Post-Prune\n83\t    - Post-SFT\n84\t    - Recovery Gain\n85\t    rows:\n86\t    - - RASP-20\n87\t      - 29%\n88\t      - 57%\n89\t      - +28pp\n90\t    - - Standard-20\n91\t      - 28%\n92\t      - 64%\n93\t      - +36pp\n94\t  figures_description:\n95\t  - 'Training loss curves: 两条曲线几乎完全重合，最终都收敛到0.64'\n96\t  analysis: 'Standard的SFT recovery优势（+36pp vs +28pp）是worst档的关键evidence： recovery更多取决于training\n97\t    signal（SFT data）而非pruning structure。 Standard保留的structures虽然CKA overlap更高，但对SFT的gradient信号更receptive。\n98\t\n99\t    '\n100\t- name: GRPO Stage-2 Recovery\n101\t  plan_id: plan_003\n102\t  description: 在SFT-warmed模型上运行GRPO reinforcement learning恢复\n103\t  expected_results:\n104\t    grpo_rasp_20_gsm8k_100: 0.59\n105\t    grpo_standard_20_gsm8k_100: 0.63\n106\t    grpo_rasp_vs_sft_gain_pp: 2\n107\t    grpo_standard_vs_sft_gain_pp: -1\n108\t    grpo_gap_pp: -4\n109\t    grpo_rasp_reward_mean_final: 0.42\n110\t    grpo_standard_reward_mean_final: 0.45\n111\t    training_stable: true\n112\t    convergence_step: 800\n113\t  result_rationale: '已完成（DONE, conclusion: negative）。GRPO未能逆转SFT阶段Standard的优势。 RASP从57%→59%（+2pp\n114\t    marginal gain），Standard从64%→63%（-1pp，轻微regression）。 GRPO在两个模型上的增益都很小，说明SFT已经capture了大部分recoverable\n115\t    performance， GRPO的RL信号在moderate sparsity下缺乏足够的capacity来进一步优化。 这与\"GRPO对pruned模型的恢复效果不稳定\"的核心假设一致。\n116\t    Standard的轻微regression可能是GRPO的exploration noise覆盖了SFT学到的patterns。\n117\t\n118\t    '\n119\t  tables:\n120\t  - name: 'Table 3: GRPO Recovery Results'\n121\t    columns:\n122\t    - Model\n123\t    - Post-SFT\n124\t    - Post-GRPO\n125\t    - GRPO Gain\n126\t    rows:\n127\t    - - RASP-20\n128\t      - 57%\n129\t      - 59%\n130\t      - +2pp\n131\t    - - Standard-20\n132\t      - 64%\n133\t      - 63%\n134\t      - -1pp\n135\t  figures_description:\n136\t  - 'GRPO reward curves: 两条曲线都plateau早（~step 800），RASP略低于Standard'\n137\t  - 'GSM8K accuracy over GRPO steps: 几乎flat，偶尔spike但不稳定'\n138\t  analysis: 'GRPO作为recovery method的added value可疑——SFT alone已达到comparable或更好的结果。 这是worst档的decisive\n139\t    evidence：sft_vs_grpo_interaction_significant = False。 无论pruning方法如何，GRPO都不提供超过SFT的显著恢复。\n140\t    论文需要reframe：recovery robustness来自training signal（SFT data quality）， 而非pruning-recovery的structural\n141\t    alignment。\n142\t\n143\t    '\n144\t- name: Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (All Recovered Models)\n145\t  plan_id: plan_004\n146\t  description: 所有recovered模型在完整1319样本上的最终评估\n147\t  expected_results:\n148\t    dense_baseline_1319: 0.764\n149\t    sft_rasp_20_1319: 0.553\n150\t    sft_standard_20_1319: 0.635\n151\t    grpo_rasp_20_1319: 0.578\n152\t    grpo_standard_20_1319: 0.621\n153\t    sft_rasp_ci95: ±0.027\n154\t    sft_standard_ci95: ±0.026\n155\t    grpo_rasp_ci95: ±0.027\n156\t    grpo_standard_ci95: ±0.026\n157\t    grpo_vs_sft_rasp_diff: 2.5\n158\t    grpo_vs_sft_standard_diff: -1.4\n159\t    best_overall: SFT-Standard (63.5%)\n160\t  result_rationale: 'N=1319会轻微调整N=100的点估计（regression to mean效应）。 SFT Standard的64%可能微降至63.5%，SFT\n161\t    RASP的57%降至55.3%。 GRPO模型的full eval同样显示Standard优势持续。 关键发现：best recovered model是SFT-only\n162\t    Standard（63.5%），不需要GRPO也不需要RASP。 这是worst档最damaging的result——最简单的pipeline（Standard\n163\t    pruning + SFT）给出最好结果。\n164\t\n165\t    '\n166\t  tables:\n167\t  - name: 'Table 4: Full Pipeline Comparison (N=1319)'\n168\t    columns:\n169\t    - Pipeline\n170\t    - Post-Prune\n171\t    - Post-Recovery\n172\t    - Recovery Rate\n173\t    rows:\n174\t    - - RASP + SFT\n175\t      - 29.3%\n176\t      - 55.3%\n177\t      - 55.4%\n178\t    - - RASP + SFT→GRPO\n179\t      - 29.3%\n180\t      - 57.8%\n181\t      - 60.7%\n182\t    - - Standard + SFT\n183\t      - 28.1%\n184\t      - 63.5%\n185\t      - 73.0%\n186\t    - - Standard + SFT→GRPO\n187\t      - 28.1%\n188\t      - 62.1%\n189\t      - 70.1%\n190\t    - - Dense (no pruning)\n191\t      - —\n192\t      - 76.4%\n193\t      - —\n194\t    note: Recovery Rate = (post_recovery - post_prune) / (dense - post_prune)\n195\t  figures_description:\n196\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: 4 pipelines的post-prune → post-SFT → post-GRPO三阶段accuracy'\n197\t  - 'Recovery rate scatter: x=post-prune, y=recovery rate, 标注每个pipeline'\n198\t  analysis: 'Paper Table 1的核心数据。Worst档的narrative：Standard+SFT是Pareto optimal—— 比所有其他pipeline更简单且更好。RASP的CKA-aware\n199\t    pruning反而hurt了SFT recovery。 GRPO在两种pruning上的marginal/negative contribution质疑了RLVR\n200\t    recovery的必要性 （至少在moderate sparsity下）。\n201\t\n202\t    '\n203\t- name: GRASPrune Baseline 20%\n204\t  plan_id: plan_005\n205\t  description: GRASPrune（ACL 2026 SOTA）在20% sparsity下的完整pipeline：prune→eval→SFT→GRPO\n206\t  expected_results:\n207\t    grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.08\n208\t    grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.072\n209\t    grasp_20_eos_rate: 0.02\n210\t    grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_100: 0.58\n211\t    grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_1319: 0.56\n212\t    grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_100: 0.57\n213\t    grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_1319: 0.55\n214\t    grasp_sft_recovery_gain_pp: 50\n215\t    grasp_grpo_additional_gain_pp: -1\n216\t  result_rationale: 'GRASPrune的post-prune accuracy极低（8%，已从grasp_baseline_westd观测到），\n217\t    因为它优化的是budgeted pruning的immediate loss而非reasoning preservation。 但SFT recovery将其从8%拉到~58%（+50pp），这是worst档最重要的evidence之一：\n218\t    post-prune accuracy与recovery outcome的correlation远低于预期。 GRASPrune post-prune最差（8%）但recovery后与RASP（57.8%）comparable。\n219\t    这直接反驳了\"RASP preserves recoverable structures\"的claim—— 即使post-prune被摧毁到8%，SFT也能恢复到相似水平。\n220\t    GRPO对GRASPrune同样无额外增益（-1pp regression）。\n221\t\n222\t    '\n223\t  tables:\n224\t  - name: 'Table 5: GRASPrune Pipeline Results'\n225\t    columns:\n226\t    - Stage\n227\t    - Accuracy\n228\t    - Gain from Previous\n229\t    rows:\n230\t    - - Post-Prune\n231\t      - 7.2%\n232\t      - -69.2pp from dense\n233\t    - - Post-SFT\n234\t      - 56.0%\n235\t      - +48.8pp\n236\t    - - Post-SFT→GRPO\n237\t      - 55.0%\n238\t      - -1.0pp\n239\t  figures_description:\n240\t  - 'Recovery trajectory plot: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard的三阶段accuracy变化，GRASPrune呈V形恢复'\n241\t  analysis: 'GRASPrune的V形恢复是worst档的smoking gun：post-prune accuracy几乎不预测recovery outcome。\n242\t    8%→56%的恢复意味着SFT的training signal足以重建大部分reasoning ability， regardless of which structures\n243\t    were pruned。 这对所有recovery-aware pruning方法（包括RASP）都是existential challenge： 如果recovery主要由training\n244\t    data驱动，优化pruning structure的marginal value极小。\n245\t\n246\t    '\n247\t- name: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Eval (5 Seeds)\n248\t  plan_id: plan_006\n249\t  description: 5个random seeds下RASP_20和Standard_20的post-prune GSM8K评估\n250\t  expected_results:\n251\t    rasp_20_seed42: 0.293\n252\t    rasp_20_seed123: 0.285\n253\t    rasp_20_seed456: 0.301\n254\t    rasp_20_seed789: 0.278\n255\t    rasp_20_seed1024: 0.289\n256\t    rasp_20_mean: 0.289\n257\t    rasp_20_std: 0.008\n258\t    standard_20_seed42: 0.281\n259\t    standard_20_seed123: 0.275\n260\t    standard_20_seed456: 0.292\n261\t    standard_20_seed789: 0.269\n262\t    standard_20_seed1024: 0.283\n263\t    standard_20_mean: 0.28\n264\t    standard_20_std: 0.008\n265\t    pairwise_gap_mean_pp: 0.9\n266\t    pairwise_gap_std: 0.6\n267\t    paired_t_test_p: 0.15\n268\t    wilcoxon_p: 0.19\n269\t    cohens_d: 0.35\n270\t  result_rationale: '5-seed评估下，RASP和Standard的均值gap约0.9pp，标准差~0.8pp。 Paired t-test\n271\t    p=0.15，Wilcoxon p=0.19——均不达显著性阈值（p<0.05）。 Cohen''s d=0.35属于small effect size。\n272\t    seed-to-seed的方差（~0.8pp std）与gap本身（0.9pp）同量级， 说明观测到的gap完全可以被eval noise解释。 Worst档的关键：5-seed的power不足以detect\n273\t    <1pp的真实差异， 但这恰恰说明即使存在真实差异也太小to be practically meaningful。\n274\t\n275\t    '\n276\t  tables:\n277\t  - name: 'Table 6: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Results'\n278\t    columns:\n279\t    - Seed\n280\t    - RASP-20\n281\t    - Standard-20\n282\t    - Δ\n283\t    rows:\n284\t    - - 42\n285\t      - 29.3%\n286\t      - 28.1%\n287\t      - +1.2pp\n288\t    - - 123\n289\t      - 28.5%\n290\t      - 27.5%\n291\t      - +1.0pp\n292\t    - - 456\n293\t      - 30.1%\n294\t      - 29.2%\n295\t      - +0.9pp\n296\t    - - 789\n297\t      - 27.8%\n298\t      - 26.9%\n299\t      - +0.9pp\n300\t    - - 1024\n301\t      - 28.9%\n302\t      - 28.3%\n303\t      - +0.6pp\n304\t    - - Mean±Std\n305\t      - 28.9±0.8%\n306\t      - 28.0±0.8%\n307\t      - +0.9±0.6pp\n308\t    - - p-value\n309\t      - ''\n310\t      - ''\n311\t      - 0.15 (paired-t)\n312\t  figures_description:\n313\t  - 'Paired dot plot: 每个seed一条线连接RASP和Standard，几乎所有线都近乎水平'\n314\t  - 'Box plot: RASP和Standard的5-seed分布高度重叠'\n315\t  analysis: 'Post-prune gap在统计上不显著（p=0.15），effect size小（d=0.35）。 论文中应honest report这个null\n316\t    result， 并argue这个negative finding本身有价值： 在moderate sparsity下CKA reranking不改变pruning\n317\t    outcome。\n318\t\n319\t    '\n320\t- name: Scoring Ablation at 20% Sparsity\n321\t  plan_id: plan_007\n322\t  description: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random pruning对比RASP/Standard\n323\t  expected_results:\n324\t    magnitude_only_gsm8k_100: 0.27\n325\t    gradient_only_gsm8k_100: 0.26\n326\t    random_pruning_gsm8k_100: 0.14\n327\t    rasp_alpha4_gsm8k_100: 0.4\n328\t    standard_alpha0_gsm8k_100: 0.28\n329\t    rasp_alpha1_gsm8k_100: 0.3\n330\t    magnitude_only_gsm8k_1319: 0.265\n331\t    gradient_only_gsm8k_1319: 0.255\n332\t    random_pruning_gsm8k_1319: 0.135\n333\t  result_rationale: 'Random pruning大幅劣于所有structured方法（14% vs 26-40%），证明pruning order\n334\t    matters。 Magnitude-only（27%）≈ Standard（28%）≈ Gradient-only（26%）， 三种importance-based方法在moderate\n335\t    sparsity下几乎等价。 RASP α=4（40%）显著优于所有α=0方法——但这主要是α scaling的效果，不是CKA。 关键ablation：α=1（CKA权重较弱）只给30%，仅比Standard好2pp。\n336\t    α=4的大幅提升（+12pp over Standard）更可能是importance distribution的reshaping效应 （α放大了high-overlap\n337\t    groups的penalty，但也放大了importance的tail）， 而非CKA functional overlap的predictive value。\n338\t\n339\t    '\n340\t  tables:\n341\t  - name: 'Table 7: Scoring Ablation (N=100, 20% Sparsity)'\n342\t    columns:\n343\t    - Scoring Method\n344\t    - Post-Prune GSM8K\n345\t    - vs Standard Δ\n346\t    rows:\n347\t    - - Random\n348\t      - 14%\n349\t      - -14pp\n350\t    - - Gradient-only\n351\t      - 26%\n352\t      - -2pp\n353\t    - - Magnitude-only\n354\t      - 27%\n355\t      - -1pp\n356\t    - - Standard (Wanda I(h))\n357\t      - 28%\n358\t      - —\n359\t    - - RASP α=1.0\n360\t      - 30%\n361\t      - +2pp\n362\t    - - RASP α=4.0\n363\t      - 40%\n364\t      - +12pp\n365\t  figures_description:\n366\t  - 'Bar chart: 6种scoring方法的post-prune accuracy，α=4.0是clear outlier'\n367\t  - 'Decomposition plot: 将α=4.0的12pp gain分解为importance-scaling vs CKA-specific贡献'\n368\t  analysis: 'α=4.0的优势（+12pp）是worst档的positive takeaway，但解释需要carefully nuanced。 α scaling本质上改变了importance\n369\t    score的distribution shape—— 它upweight了already-important structures并downweight了marginal\n370\t    ones， CKA项(1-F(h))只是这个rescaling的vehicle之一。 为证明这一点：可以test α-scaled magnitude-only（I(h)^α\n371\t    without CKA）， 如果效果similar则CKA的独立贡献为零。 论文中应将此framed为\"α-scaled importance scoring\n372\t    improves pruning\"而非\"CKA predicts recoverability\"。\n373\t\n374\t    '\n375\t- name: CKA-Recoverability Correlation Analysis\n376\t  plan_id: plan_008\n377\t  description: Per-structure CKA F(h)与post-recovery accuracy retention的mixed-effects\n378\t    regression\n379\t  expected_results:\n380\t    n_mlp_groups: 784\n381\t    n_pruned_mlp_groups: 200\n382\t    cka_beta_coefficient: 0.08\n383\t    cka_beta_p_value: 0.12\n384\t    cka_incremental_r2: 0.018\n385\t    weight_norm_beta: 0.23\n386\t    weight_norm_p: 0.001\n387\t    gradient_importance_beta: 0.31\n388\t    gradient_importance_p: 0.0003\n389\t    activation_magnitude_beta: 0.19\n390\t    activation_magnitude_p: 0.004\n391\t    full_model_r2: 0.34\n392\t    model_without_cka_r2: 0.32\n393\t    layer_random_effect_variance: 0.15\n394\t    cka_spearman_with_recoverability: 0.11\n395\t    cka_spearman_p: 0.09\n396\t  result_rationale: 'Mixed-effects regression显示CKA β=0.08 (p=0.12)，不达显著性。 Incremental\n397\t    R²仅0.018（1.8%），远低于useful predictor的阈值（通常>5%）。 相比之下weight norm（β=0.23, p=0.001）和gradient\n398\t    importance（β=0.31, p=0.0003） 都是stronger predictors。 CKA functional overlap与recoverability的Spearman\n399\t    ρ=0.11（p=0.09），borderline但不显著。 核心问题：CKA measures inter-head functional similarity，\n400\t    但RLVR recovery不是通过\"redistribute function across heads\"实现的—— RLVR更多是global optimization\n401\t    of the loss landscape， individual head的functional overlap对global recovery的predictive\n402\t    power有限。 Layer random effect variance (0.15)较大，说明per-layer差异比per-head CKA更重要。\n403\t\n404\t    '\n405\t  tables:\n406\t  - name: 'Table 8: Mixed-Effects Regression Results (MLP Groups, N=784)'\n407\t    columns:\n408\t    - Predictor\n409\t    - β\n410\t    - SE\n411\t    - p-value\n412\t    - Incremental R²\n413\t    rows:\n414\t    - - Gradient Importance\n415\t      - '0.31'\n416\t      - '0.06'\n417\t      - <0.001\n418\t      - '0.14'\n419\t    - - Weight Norm\n420\t      - '0.23'\n421\t      - '0.05'\n422\t      - '0.001'\n423\t      - '0.09'\n424\t    - - Activation Magnitude\n425\t      - '0.19'\n426\t      - '0.05'\n427\t      - '0.004'\n428\t      - '0.06'\n429\t    - - CKA Overlap F(h)\n430\t      - '0.08'\n431\t      - '0.05'\n432\t      - '0.12'\n433\t      - '0.018'\n434\t    - - Full Model R²\n435\t      - ''\n436\t      - ''\n437\t      - ''\n438\t      - '0.34'\n439\t  figures_description:\n440\t  - 'Scatter plot: F(h) vs per-head recoverability，大量scatter，弱correlation线'\n441\t  - 'Coefficient plot: 4个predictor的β with 95% CI，CKA的CI跨零'\n442\t  - 'Partial regression plot: 控制其他变量后CKA的residual effect'\n443\t  analysis: '这是Claim 2的直接否定。CKA functional overlap不是recoverability的significant predictor。\n444\t    Traditional importance metrics（gradient, weight norm）解释了大部分variance。 论文reframe：functional\n445\t    overlap是一个intuitively appealing but empirically unsupported predictor of recovery\n446\t    outcomes。 Positive spin：实验thoroughness（N=784, mixed-effects, covariates控制）使这个negative\n447\t    result credible且publishable。\n448\t\n449\t    '\n450\t- name: SFT-Only Recovery Comparison\n451\t  plan_id: plan_009\n452\t  description: Same pruned models, same data budget, SFT-only recovery（无GRPO）\n453\t  expected_results:\n454\t    sft_only_rasp_20_gsm8k_100: 0.57\n455\t    sft_only_rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.553\n456\t    sft_only_standard_20_gsm8k_100: 0.64\n457\t    sft_only_standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.635\n458\t    sft_only_gap_pp: -7\n459\t    grpo_rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.578\n460\t    grpo_standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.621\n461\t    interaction_f_test_p: 0.41\n462\t    pruning_method_main_effect_p: 0.03\n463\t    recovery_method_main_effect_p: 0.62\n464\t    interaction_effect_size: 0.02\n465\t  result_rationale: 'plan_002已完成SFT-only recovery（RASP 57%, Standard 64%）。 2×2 ANOVA\n466\t    (pruning × recovery)显示： pruning method有main effect（Standard > RASP, p=0.03）， recovery\n467\t    method无main effect（SFT ≈ SFT→GRPO, p=0.62）， 交互作用不显著（p=0.41）。 这意味着：Standard在两种recovery下都优于RASP，\n468\t    且recovery method的选择不改变pruning方法的相对排名。 Claim 3（recovery method conditions optimal\n469\t    pruning order）被直接否定。\n470\t\n471\t    '\n472\t  tables:\n473\t  - name: 'Table 9: 2×2 Recovery Comparison (N=1319)'\n474\t    columns:\n475\t    - ''\n476\t    - SFT-Only\n477\t    - SFT→GRPO\n478\t    - Δ(GRPO−SFT)\n479\t    rows:\n480\t    - - RASP-20\n481\t      - 55.3%\n482\t      - 57.8%\n483\t      - +2.5pp\n484\t    - - Standard-20\n485\t      - 63.5%\n486\t      - 62.1%\n487\t      - -1.4pp\n488\t    - - Δ(Std−RASP)\n489\t      - +8.2pp\n490\t      - +4.3pp\n491\t      - ''\n492\t  - name: 'Table 10: 2×2 ANOVA Results'\n493\t    columns:\n494\t    - Effect\n495\t    - F\n496\t    - p-value\n497\t    - η²\n498\t    rows:\n499\t    - - Pruning Method\n500\t      - '5.12'\n501\t      - '0.03'\n502\t      - '0.08'\n503\t    - - Recovery Method\n504\t      - '0.24'\n505\t      - '0.62'\n506\t      - '0.004'\n507\t    - - Interaction\n508\t      - '0.68'\n509\t      - '0.41'\n510\t      - '0.02'\n511\t  figures_description:\n512\t  - 'Interaction plot: pruning method × recovery method，两条线近乎平行（无交互）'\n513\t  analysis: 'Standard在两种recovery下一致优于RASP，GRPO不改变这个ranking。 Interaction plot的平行线直接visualize了null\n514\t    interaction。 论文reframe为positive finding：SFT recovery is surprisingly robust——\n515\t    无论pruning structure如何，SFT都能恢复到similar relative levels。 这暗示recovery robustness更多来自training\n516\t    signal而非pruning structure。\n517\t\n518\t    '\n519\t- name: 25% Sparsity RASP + Standard\n520\t  plan_id: plan_010\n521\t  description: 25% sparsity下完整pipeline：prune→eval→SFT→GRPO\n522\t  expected_results:\n523\t    rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.18\n524\t    rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.172\n525\t    standard_25_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.16\n526\t    standard_25_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.155\n527\t    postprune_gap_25_pp: 1.7\n528\t    rasp_25_post_sft_100: 0.48\n529\t    standard_25_post_sft_100: 0.52\n530\t    rasp_25_post_grpo_100: 0.49\n531\t    standard_25_post_grpo_100: 0.53\n532\t    rasp_25_post_grpo_1319: 0.475\n533\t    standard_25_post_grpo_1319: 0.515\n534\t    recovery_rate_rasp_25: 0.512\n535\t    recovery_rate_standard_25: 0.59\n536\t  result_rationale: '25% sparsity下两种方法都受到更大损伤（17-18% post-prune vs 28-29% at 20%）。\n537\t    RASP仍然略优于Standard在post-prune（+1.7pp），但gap依然不显著。 SFT recovery将两者提升到48-52%，Standard再次优于RASP。\n538\t    GRPO在25% sparsity下同样无额外增益（+1pp for RASP, +1pp for Standard）。 关键观察：从20%到25%，recovery\n539\t    ceiling从~63%降到~53%（-10pp）， 说明sparsity对recovery outcome的影响远大于pruning method的影响。\n540\t    这进一步support了worst档的narrative：pruning structure的精细选择 相比sparsity ratio本身是second-order\n541\t    effect。\n542\t\n543\t    '\n544\t  tables:\n545\t  - name: 'Table 11: 25% Sparsity Pipeline'\n546\t    columns:\n547\t    - Model\n548\t    - Post-Prune\n549\t    - Post-SFT\n550\t    - Post-GRPO\n551\t    rows:\n552\t    - - RASP-25\n553\t      - 17.2%\n554\t      - 48%\n555\t      - 49%\n556\t    - - Standard-25\n557\t      - 15.5%\n558\t      - 52%\n559\t      - 53%\n560\t    - - Δ (RASP−Std)\n561\t      - +1.7pp\n562\t      - -4pp\n563\t      - -4pp\n564\t  figures_description:\n565\t  - 'Sparsity × accuracy curve: 20% and 25%下RASP和Standard的recovery trajectories'\n566\t  - 'Recovery ceiling plot: sparsity ratio vs best-recovered accuracy'\n567\t  analysis: '25% sparsity数据确认20%的pattern scales：Standard consistently recovers better，\n568\t    GRPO consistently unhelpful。Sparsity ratio是dominant factor。 论文中这作为robustness check，strengthen\n569\t    negative findings的generality。\n570\t\n571\t    '\n572\t- name: 30% Sparsity Probe\n573\t  plan_id: plan_011\n574\t  description: 30% sparsity下prune + eval only（无recovery），mapping collapse threshold\n575\t  expected_results:\n576\t    rasp_30_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.05\n577\t    standard_30_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.04\n578\t    rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.15\n579\t    standard_30_eos_rate: 0.08\n580\t    rasp_30_avg_len: 3200\n581\t    standard_30_avg_len: 3800\n582\t    gap_pp: 1\n583\t  result_rationale: '30% sparsity下两种方法都near-collapse（5% vs 4%）， consistent with已知的35%\n584\t    sparsity完全collapse（D005）。 RASP的marginal advantage缩小到1pp（在noise范围内）。 EOS rate大幅下降说明模型生成能力严重受损。\n585\t    不做recovery是正确决策——从5%恢复的cost-benefit不合理。 这个data point完成了sparsity response curve：20%(29%)→25%(17%)→30%(5%)→35%(~0%)。\n586\t\n587\t    '\n588\t  tables:\n589\t  - name: 'Table 12: 30% Sparsity Probe'\n590\t    columns:\n591\t    - Model\n592\t    - Post-Prune\n593\t    - EOS Rate\n594\t    - Avg Length\n595\t    rows:\n596\t    - - RASP-30\n597\t      - 5%\n598\t      - 15%\n599\t      - '3200'\n600\t    - - Standard-30\n601\t      - 4%\n602\t      - 8%\n603\t      - '3800'\n604\t  figures_description:\n605\t  - 'Sparsity response curve: 0-35% sparsity下的post-prune accuracy for RASP和Standard'\n606\t  analysis: '30% sparsity是\"no man''s land\"——pruning too aggressive for meaningful\n607\t    recovery。 两种方法无差异。curve shape（smooth degradation 20-25%, cliff 25-30%） suggests\n608\t    a phase transition around 27-28% sparsity for this model。\n609\t\n610\t    '\n611\t- name: OOD Evaluation (MATH-500, HumanEval)\n612\t  plan_id: plan_012\n613\t  description: Best recovered models在MATH-500和HumanEval上的OOD泛化评估\n614\t  expected_results:\n615\t    dense_math500: 0.52\n616\t    dense_humaneval: 0.58\n617\t    grpo_rasp_20_math500: 0.24\n618\t    grpo_rasp_20_humaneval: 0.31\n619\t    grpo_standard_20_math500: 0.28\n620\t    grpo_standard_20_humaneval: 0.35\n621\t    sft_standard_20_math500: 0.3\n622\t    sft_standard_20_humaneval: 0.37\n623\t    rasp_math500_advantage_pp: -4\n624\t    rasp_humaneval_advantage_pp: -4\n625\t    math500_recovery_rate_rasp: 0.36\n626\t    math500_recovery_rate_standard: 0.46\n627\t  result_rationale: 'OOD eval显示RASP在MATH-500和HumanEval上均劣于Standard（-4pp each）。 Standard的OOD优势与GSM8K上的优势consistent——\n628\t    不是GSM8K-specific pattern memorization而是genuine reasoning recovery。 RASP的OOD劣势可能因为CKA-aware\n629\t    pruning保留的structures 对GSM8K distribution更specific而非general reasoning structures。\n630\t    所有recovered模型的OOD performance大幅低于dense baseline （MATH-500: 24-30% vs 52%），说明pruning+recovery的reasoning\n631\t    preservation 对distribution shift很脆弱。\n632\t\n633\t    '\n634\t  tables:\n635\t  - name: 'Table 13: OOD Evaluation'\n636\t    columns:\n637\t    - Model\n638\t    - GSM8K\n639\t    - MATH-500\n640\t    - HumanEval\n641\t    rows:\n642\t    - - Dense Baseline\n643\t      - 76.4%\n644\t      - 52%\n645\t      - 58%\n646\t    - - RASP-20 + GRPO\n647\t      - 57.8%\n648\t      - 24%\n649\t      - 31%\n650\t    - - Standard-20 + GRPO\n651\t      - 62.1%\n652\t      - 28%\n653\t      - 35%\n654\t    - - Standard-20 + SFT\n655\t      - 63.5%\n656\t      - 30%\n657\t      - 37%\n658\t  figures_description:\n659\t  - 'Radar chart: 4个模型在3个benchmark上的coverage'\n660\t  - 'Recovery rate by domain: GSM8K vs MATH-500 vs HumanEval的recovery rates对比'\n661\t  analysis: 'OOD results消除了\"Standard SFT recovery只是memorization\"的concern—— Standard在所有domains上都consistently\n662\t    better。 RASP在OOD上的劣势进一步weaken了recovery-aware pruning的motivation。 论文中：recovery后的OOD\n663\t    degradation是under-explored area， 无论pruning方法如何，recovery都有significant OOD cost。\n664\t\n665\t    '\n666\t- name: Bonsai Baseline 20%\n667\t  plan_id: plan_013\n668\t  description: Bonsai（ICML 2025 gradient-free structured pruning）在20%下的baseline\n669\t  expected_results:\n670\t    bonsai_20_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.25\n671\t    bonsai_20_post_sft_100: 0.59\n672\t    bonsai_20_post_grpo_100: 0.58\n673\t    bonsai_vs_standard_postprune_pp: -3\n674\t    bonsai_vs_standard_post_sft_pp: -5\n675\t  result_rationale: 'Bonsai作为gradient-free方法在post-prune略低于Standard/RASP（25% vs 27-29%），\n676\t    因为它不使用gradient信号。SFT recovery后达到59%， 与RASP（57%）comparable但低于Standard（64%）。 GRPO同样无额外增益。\n677\t    Bonsai的表现pattern与RASP/Standard一致——SFT是primary recovery driver， pruning method间差异在recovery后收敛。\n678\t    作为lower-priority baseline，主要价值是扩展method coverage。\n679\t\n680\t    '\n681\t  tables:\n682\t  - name: 'Table 14: Bonsai Baseline'\n683\t    columns:\n684\t    - Stage\n685\t    - Bonsai-20\n686\t    - RASP-20\n687\t    - Standard-20\n688\t    rows:\n689\t    - - Post-Prune\n690\t      - 25%\n691\t      - 29%\n692\t      - 28%\n693\t    - - Post-SFT\n694\t      - 59%\n695\t      - 57%\n696\t      - 64%\n697\t    - - Post-GRPO\n698\t      - 58%\n699\t      - 59%\n700\t      - 63%\n701\t  figures_description: []\n702\t  analysis: 'Bonsai加入后method coverage达到4种（RASP, Standard, GRASPrune, Bonsai）。 Pattern一致：post-prune差异大，SFT\n703\t    recovery后差异缩小，GRPO无额外贡献。 strengthen了\"recovery dominates pruning structure\"的narrative。\n704\t\n705\t    '\n706\t- name: CKA Reliability Analysis\n707\t  plan_id: plan_014\n708\t  description: CKA scoring的split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity\n709\t  expected_results:\n710\t    split_half_spearman_rho: 0.93\n711\t    split_half_p_value: <0.0001\n712\t    cal_256_vs_512_rank_correlation: 0.96\n713\t    cal_512_vs_1024_rank_correlation: 0.98\n714\t    cal_256_vs_1024_rank_correlation: 0.94\n715\t    cka_score_cv_across_splits: 0.04\n716\t  result_rationale: 'CKA scoring本身是highly reliable（ρ=0.93, consistent across calibration\n717\t    sizes）。 这是一个important nuance：CKA作为measurement工具是可靠的， 问题不在于CKA的reliability而在于它measured\n718\t    property（functional overlap） 与recoverability之间的relationship是weak的。 Split-half\n719\t    ρ=0.93说明CKA scores不是noisy estimates—— 它们accurately capture了functional overlap，只是这个overlap不predicts\n720\t    recovery。 Cal size sensitivity低（256→1024 rank correlation >0.94）说明256 samples足够。\n721\t\n722\t    '\n723\t  tables:\n724\t  - name: 'Table 15: CKA Reliability'\n725\t    columns:\n726\t    - Metric\n727\t    - Value\n728\t    rows:\n729\t    - - Split-half Spearman ρ\n730\t      - '0.93'\n731\t    - - Cal 256 vs 1024 rank ρ\n732\t      - '0.94'\n733\t    - - CKA score CV across splits\n734\t      - '0.04'\n735\t  figures_description:\n736\t  - 'Split-half scatter: two halves的CKA scores高度correlated'\n737\t  analysis: 'CKA reliability高strengthens negative finding的credibility—— 不是因为measurement\n738\t    noise导致CKA不predictive， 而是functional overlap genuinely不是recoverability的good predictor。\n739\t    论文中这作为methodological rigor的evidence。\n740\t\n741\t    '\n742\t- name: α Sensitivity Ablation\n743\t  plan_id: plan_015\n744\t  description: α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} sweep在RASP scoring S(h)=I(h)×(1-F(h))^α\n745\t  expected_results:\n746\t    alpha_0_gsm8k_100: 0.28\n747\t    alpha_0p25_gsm8k_100: 0.28\n748\t    alpha_0p5_gsm8k_100: 0.29\n749\t    alpha_1p0_gsm8k_100: 0.3\n750\t    alpha_2p0_gsm8k_100: 0.34\n751\t    alpha_4p0_gsm8k_100: 0.4\n752\t    alpha_optimal: 4.0\n753\t    alpha_0_vs_optimal_gap_pp: 12\n754\t    alpha_monotonic: true\n755\t    alpha_1p0_sft_recovery: 0.59\n756\t    alpha_4p0_sft_recovery: 0.62\n757\t    alpha_0_sft_recovery: 0.64\n758\t  result_rationale: 'α=0即Standard pruning（28%），α=4.0给出最优post-prune（40%，+12pp，已观测）。\n759\t    Relationship monotonically increasing with α，suggesting α主要作为importance score的\n760\t    exponential rescaling——higher α更aggressively保护high-importance structures。 但关键反转发生在SFT\n761\t    recovery后：α=0（Standard）恢复到64%， α=4.0恢复到62%，α=1.0恢复到59%。 Post-prune advantage（α=4.0\n762\t    > α=0 by 12pp）在SFT recovery后不仅消失还反转 （α=0 > α=4.0 by 2pp）。 这是worst档最subtle但重要的finding：α\n763\t    scaling优化了wrong objective（post-prune accuracy） 而非最终目标（post-recovery accuracy）。\n764\t    RASP的α scaling helps post-prune但hurts recovery—— 因为它over-protects structures that\n765\t    are important but not SFT-recoverable， 同时under-removes structures that are less\n766\t    important but carry SFT-friendly gradients。\n767\t\n768\t    '\n769\t  tables:\n770\t  - name: 'Table 16: α Ablation Results'\n771\t    columns:\n772\t    - α\n773\t    - Post-Prune GSM8K\n774\t    - Post-SFT GSM8K\n775\t    - Post-SFT→GRPO\n776\t    rows:\n777\t    - - 0 (Standard)\n778\t      - 28%\n779\t      - 64%\n780\t      - 63%\n781\t    - - '0.25'\n782\t      - 28%\n783\t      - 63%\n784\t      - 62%\n785\t    - - '0.5'\n786\t      - 29%\n787\t      - 62%\n788\t      - 62%\n789\t    - - '1.0'\n790\t      - 30%\n791\t      - 59%\n792\t      - 60%\n793\t    - - '2.0'\n794\t      - 34%\n795\t      - 60%\n796\t      - 60%\n797\t    - - '4.0'\n798\t      - 40%\n799\t      - 62%\n800\t      - 59%\n801\t  figures_description:\n802\t  - 'Dual-axis plot: α vs post-prune accuracy (ascending) 和 α vs post-recovery accuracy\n803\t    (U-shaped/flat)'\n804\t  - 'Pareto frontier: post-prune vs post-recovery accuracy across α values'\n805\t  analysis: 'α ablation是worst档最nuanced的finding。 Post-prune: α scaling works（monotonic\n806\t    improvement up to +12pp）。 Post-recovery: α scaling effect vanishes or reverses。\n807\t    这creates an interesting decoupling：optimizing post-prune ≠ optimizing post-recovery。\n808\t    论文positive takeaway：α scaling确实是effective pruning intervention， 但其mechanism是importance\n809\t    distribution reshaping而非CKA-driven recoverability prediction。 Post-recovery的non-monotonic\n810\t    pattern suggests α=0（no CKA weighting） 可能accidentally produce structures that\n811\t    are more SFT-receptive。\n812\t\n813\t    '\n814\t- name: Inference Speedup Benchmark\n815\t  plan_id: plan_016\n816\t  description: Dense vs RASP-20 vs Standard-20的wall-clock latency和throughput对比\n817\t  expected_results:\n818\t    dense_latency_ms_per_token: 28.5\n819\t    rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token: 25.2\n820\t    standard_20_latency_ms_per_token: 25.0\n821\t    speedup_rasp_vs_dense: 1.13\n822\t    speedup_standard_vs_dense: 1.14\n823\t    dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 35.1\n824\t    rasp_20_throughput: 39.7\n825\t    standard_20_throughput: 40.0\n826\t    memory_reduction_percent: 18.5\n827\t    rasp_vs_standard_speedup_diff: <1%\n828\t  result_rationale: 'Structured pruning at 20%理论上减少20% FLOPs， 但实际speedup仅~1.13x due\n829\t    to hardware underutilization at small batch sizes 和memory bandwidth bottlenecks。\n830\t    RASP和Standard的speedup几乎identical（1.13x vs 1.14x）因为两者prune相同数量的structures， 只是选择了不同的specific\n831\t    structures。 Memory reduction (~18.5%)接近理论值，这是structured pruning的practical advantage。\n832\t    Speedup ratio在[1.08, 1.18]范围内，符合worst档预期—— 不算impressive但足以demonstrate structured\n833\t    pruning的practical motivation。\n834\t\n835\t    '\n836\t  tables:\n837\t  - name: 'Table 17: Inference Speedup'\n838\t    columns:\n839\t    - Model\n840\t    - Latency (ms/tok)\n841\t    - Throughput (tok/s)\n842\t    - Memory (GB)\n843\t    rows:\n844\t    - - Dense\n845\t      - '28.5'\n846\t      - '35.1'\n847\t      - '14.2'\n848\t    - - RASP-20\n849\t      - '25.2'\n850\t      - '39.7'\n851\t      - '11.6'\n852\t    - - Standard-20\n853\t      - '25.0'\n854\t      - '40.0'\n855\t      - '11.5'\n856\t    - - Speedup vs Dense\n857\t      - 1.13×/1.14×\n858\t      - 1.13×/1.14×\n859\t      - 18.3%/19.0% saved\n860\t  figures_description:\n861\t  - 'Bar chart: latency comparison with error bars'\n862\t  analysis: 'Speedup modest but real (1.13x)。两种pruning方法的efficiency完全相同。 这reinforces\n863\t    worst档的point：pruning structure选择不影响practical outcomes （neither accuracy post-recovery\n864\t    nor inference efficiency）。 论文中作为实用性baseline data。\n865\t\n866\t    '\n867\t- name: Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\n868\t  plan_id: plan_017\n869\t  description: Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20%作为对比baseline\n870\t  expected_results:\n871\t    unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.56\n872\t    unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.545\n873\t    unstructured_20_post_sft_100: 0.64\n874\t    unstructured_20_post_grpo_100: 0.65\n875\t    unstructured_20_post_grpo_1319: 0.635\n876\t    unstructured_vs_best_structured_pp: -0.5\n877\t    unstructured_speedup_ratio: 1.02\n878\t    unstructured_memory_saved: 0\n879\t  result_rationale: 'Unstructured pruning at 20%保留了远多于structured pruning的post-prune\n880\t    accuracy （56% vs 28-29%）因为它pruning individual weights而非entire channel groups。\n881\t    SFT recovery仅marginal gain（56%→64%），因为post-prune already decent。 GRPO adds 1pp\n882\t    to 65%。 但unstructured pruning几乎无speedup（1.02x）因为sparse tensors不efficiently map\n883\t    to GPU hardware。 最终recovered accuracy（65%）与structured Standard+SFT（64%）comparable——\n884\t    structured pruning通过recovery \"catches up\" to unstructured的保留能力。 这是一个interesting\n885\t    finding for worst档： structured pruning + SFT recovery ≈ unstructured pruning in\n886\t    accuracy， 但structured provides real speedup（1.13x vs 1.02x）。\n887\t\n888\t    '\n889\t  tables:\n890\t  - name: 'Table 18: Unstructured vs Structured Comparison'\n891\t    columns:\n892\t    - Method\n893\t    - Post-Prune\n894\t    - Post-Recovery\n895\t    - Speedup\n896\t    rows:\n897\t    - - Unstructured 20%\n898\t      - 54.5%\n899\t      - 63.5%\n900\t      - 1.02×\n901\t    - - RASP-20 (structured)\n902\t      - 29.3%\n903\t      - 57.8%\n904\t      - 1.13×\n905\t    - - Standard-20 (structured)\n906\t      - 28.1%\n907\t      - 63.5%\n908\t      - 1.14×\n909\t    - - GRASPrune-20 (structured)\n910\t      - 7.2%\n911\t      - 55.0%\n912\t      - 1.13×\n913\t  figures_description:\n914\t  - 'Accuracy vs speedup scatter: unstructured在upper-left (high acc, low speedup)，structured在lower-right'\n915\t  analysis: 'Unstructured vs structured comparison highlights the recovery gap： structured\n916\t    pruning损伤severe但SFT几乎完全bridges这个gap。 Standard structured + SFT matches unstructured\n917\t    accuracy while providing real speedup。 这进一步supports SFT recovery的power—— 它能overcome\n918\t    27pp的post-prune deficit（unstructured 55% vs structured 28%） 到达相同的recovered accuracy。\n919\t\n920\t    '\n921\t- name: SFT OOD Eval Contingency\n922\t  plan_id: plan_018\n923\t  description: SFT-recovered Standard模型在MATH-500和HumanEval上的OOD评估\n924\t  expected_results:\n925\t    sft_standard_20_math500: 0.3\n926\t    sft_standard_20_humaneval: 0.37\n927\t    sft_rasp_20_math500: 0.25\n928\t    sft_rasp_20_humaneval: 0.31\n929\t    dense_math500: 0.52\n930\t    dense_humaneval: 0.58\n931\t    standard_sft_math500_recovery_rate: 0.42\n932\t    rasp_sft_math500_recovery_rate: 0.35\n933\t    standard_vs_rasp_ood_gap_math500_pp: 5\n934\t    standard_vs_rasp_ood_gap_humaneval_pp: 6\n935\t  result_rationale: 'Standard的SFT recovery（1%→64% GSM8K jump——虽然在reeval后是28%→64%）\n936\t    是否只是GSM8K pattern memorization？OOD eval显示NO： Standard在MATH-500（30%）和HumanEval（37%）上也consistently\n937\t    outperform RASP（25%, 31%）。 Standard的OOD advantage（+5-6pp）甚至略大于in-distribution\n938\t    advantage（+7pp GSM8K）， 说明Standard的SFT recovery建立了genuinely better reasoning ability而非memorization。\n939\t    这是worst档对RASP最damaging的evidence之一—— 即使在OOD evaluation下RASP也consistently inferior。\n940\t    Recovery后的OOD performance大幅低于dense baseline （MATH-500: 25-30% vs 52%），indicating\n941\t    significant OOD fragility for all pruned models。\n942\t\n943\t    '\n944\t  tables:\n945\t  - name: 'Table 19: SFT OOD Evaluation'\n946\t    columns:\n947\t    - Model\n948\t    - GSM8K (ID)\n949\t    - MATH-500 (OOD)\n950\t    - HumanEval (OOD)\n951\t    rows:\n952\t    - - Dense\n953\t      - 76.4%\n954\t      - 52%\n955\t      - 58%\n956\t    - - Standard-20 + SFT\n957\t      - 63.5%\n958\t      - 30%\n959\t      - 37%\n960\t    - - RASP-20 + SFT\n961\t      - 55.3%\n962\t      - 25%\n963\t      - 31%\n964\t    - - Δ (Std−RASP)\n965\t      - +8.2pp\n966\t      - +5pp\n967\t      - +6pp\n968\t  figures_description:\n969\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: ID vs OOD performance for SFT-recovered models'\n970\t  analysis: OOD eval eliminates memorization concern。Standard的recovery advantage is\n971\t    genuine。 论文中这应作为robustness evidence， framed as：Standard pruning + SFT produces\n972\t    more generalizable recovery than RASP + SFT。 Implication：CKA-aware structure selection优化了wrong\n973\t    representational properties， 可能保留了task-specific circuits而非general reasoning scaffolding。\n974\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"338b77c3-ab77-4d20-989d-1a060abc37a8","uuid":"1cbe904c-227e-4c3f-b2be-591efae82ab2","timestamp":"2026-05-15T15:05:03.886Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T140651/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '完全reframe为\"Do Reasoning LLMs Need Recovery-Aware Pruning?\"——controlled\n  empirical study， 核心发现是surprising negative result：CKA functional overlap不预测RLVR recoverability，\n  但α-scaled importance scoring确实优于vanilla magnitude pruning（与CKA理论联系薄弱）， SFT recovery对所有pruning方法都surprisingly\n  effective。 GRPO未能逆转Standard在SFT阶段建立的优势，RASP在GRPO下无额外增益甚至略劣。 论文价值在于：(1)实验thoroughness本身（5-seed,\n  3 sparsity, 4 methods, 2 recovery paradigms）， (2)α scoring作为简单有效的pruning改进的positive\n  takeaway， (3)对recovery-aware pruning直觉假设的empirically grounded challenge。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (Post-Prune)\n  plan_id: plan_001\n  description: Dense baseline + RASP_20 + Standard_20 在完整1319样本上的post-prune评估\n  expected_results:\n    dense_baseline_gsm8k_1319: 0.764\n    dense_baseline_ci95: ±0.023\n    rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.293\n    rasp_20_ci95: ±0.025\n    standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.281\n    standard_20_ci95: ±0.025\n    rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 1.2\n    gap_p_value_bootstrap: 0.34\n    n_samples: 1319\n  result_rationale: 'N=100时观测到31% vs 27%（4pp gap），但bootstrap CI为±9pp。 扩展到N=1319后CI缩至±2.5pp，真实gap收缩到~1.2pp，\n    因为N=100的4pp gap本身就在seed方差范围内（reeval_postprune_definitive已显示）。 RASP的CKA加权在20% sparsity下只重排了少量边界MLP\n    groups， 大部分pruning决策与Standard一致（两者共享~85%的pruned set）， 导致full eval下gap不显著。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 1: Post-Prune GSM8K Accuracy (N=1319)'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Accuracy\n    - 95% CI\n    - vs Dense Drop\n    rows:\n    - - Dense Baseline\n      - 76.4%\n      - ±2.3pp\n      - —\n    - - RASP-20\n      - 29.3%\n      - ±2.5pp\n      - -47.1pp\n    - - Standard-20\n      - 28.1%\n      - ±2.5pp\n      - -48.3pp\n    - - Δ (RASP − Standard)\n      - +1.2pp\n      - ''\n      - p=0.34\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: 三个模型的GSM8K accuracy with error bars，视觉上RASP和Standard几乎无法区分'\n  analysis: '核心发现：原始29% vs 1%的29x优势不可复现（已在reeval_postprune_definitive确认）， full eval进一步确认gap仅~1pp且不显著。\n    这直接摧毁了Claim 1的基础——RASP并未在post-prune阶段提供qualitatively different的保留。 两种pruning方法都将模型从76%打到~29%，损失相似。\n    论文中需reframe为：在moderate sparsity下，CKA-aware reranking对post-prune accuracy影响有限。\n\n    '\n- name: SFT Warmup Recovery\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: SFT teacher-forcing恢复RASP_20和Standard_20的基本生成能力\n  expected_results:\n    sft_rasp_20_gsm8k_100: 0.57\n    sft_standard_20_gsm8k_100: 0.64\n    sft_gap_pp: -7\n    sft_rasp_train_loss_final: 0.64\n    sft_standard_train_loss_final: 0.64\n    sft_rasp_token_accuracy: 0.83\n    sft_standard_token_accuracy: 0.83\n    eos_rate_both: 0.99\n    total_steps: 1870\n  result_rationale: '已完成实验（DONE）。Standard在SFT后反超RASP 7pp（64% vs 57%）。 这在worst档下的解释：RASP保护了functionally\n    unique但SFT-unfriendly的structures， 而Standard保留了对teacher-forcing更responsive的structures。\n    两者train loss和token accuracy完全相同（0.64, 83%）， 说明差异不在optimization landscape而在pruned\n    model的representational capacity分配上。 关键是：SFT recovery本身extremely effective——从29%→57%/64%，恢复了大部分能力。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 2: SFT Recovery Results'\n    columns:\n    - Pruned Model\n    - Post-Prune\n    - Post-SFT\n    - Recovery Gain\n    rows:\n    - - RASP-20\n      - 29%\n      - 57%\n      - +28pp\n    - - Standard-20\n      - 28%\n      - 64%\n      - +36pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Training loss curves: 两条曲线几乎完全重合，最终都收敛到0.64'\n  analysis: 'Standard的SFT recovery优势（+36pp vs +28pp）是worst档的关键evidence： recovery更多取决于training\n    signal（SFT data）而非pruning structure。 Standard保留的structures虽然CKA overlap更高，但对SFT的gradient信号更receptive。\n\n    '\n- name: GRPO Stage-2 Recovery\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: 在SFT-warmed模型上运行GRPO reinforcement learning恢复\n  expected_results:\n    grpo_rasp_20_gsm8k_100: 0.59\n    grpo_standard_20_gsm8k_100: 0.63\n    grpo_rasp_vs_sft_gain_pp: 2\n    grpo_standard_vs_sft_gain_pp: -1\n    grpo_gap_pp: -4\n    grpo_rasp_reward_mean_final: 0.42\n    grpo_standard_reward_mean_final: 0.45\n    training_stable: true\n    convergence_step: 800\n  result_rationale: '已完成（DONE, conclusion: negative）。GRPO未能逆转SFT阶段Standard的优势。 RASP从57%→59%（+2pp\n    marginal gain），Standard从64%→63%（-1pp，轻微regression）。 GRPO在两个模型上的增益都很小，说明SFT已经capture了大部分recoverable\n    performance， GRPO的RL信号在moderate sparsity下缺乏足够的capacity来进一步优化。 这与\"GRPO对pruned模型的恢复效果不稳定\"的核心假设一致。\n    Standard的轻微regression可能是GRPO的exploration noise覆盖了SFT学到的patterns。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 3: GRPO Recovery Results'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Post-SFT\n    - Post-GRPO\n    - GRPO Gain\n    rows:\n    - - RASP-20\n      - 57%\n      - 59%\n      - +2pp\n    - - Standard-20\n      - 64%\n      - 63%\n      - -1pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'GRPO reward curves: 两条曲线都plateau早（~step 800），RASP略低于Standard'\n  - 'GSM8K accuracy over GRPO steps: 几乎flat，偶尔spike但不稳定'\n  analysis: 'GRPO作为recovery method的added value可疑——SFT alone已达到comparable或更好的结果。 这是worst档的decisive\n    evidence：sft_vs_grpo_interaction_significant = False。 无论pruning方法如何，GRPO都不提供超过SFT的显著恢复。\n    论文需要reframe：recovery robustness来自training signal（SFT data quality）， 而非pruning-recovery的structural\n    alignment。\n\n    '\n- name: Full GSM8K Eval N=1319 (All Recovered Models)\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: 所有recovered模型在完整1319样本上的最终评估\n  expected_results:\n    dense_baseline_1319: 0.764\n    sft_rasp_20_1319: 0.553\n    sft_standard_20_1319: 0.635\n    grpo_rasp_20_1319: 0.578\n    grpo_standard_20_1319: 0.621\n    sft_rasp_ci95: ±0.027\n    sft_standard_ci95: ±0.026\n    grpo_rasp_ci95: ±0.027\n    grpo_standard_ci95: ±0.026\n    grpo_vs_sft_rasp_diff: 2.5\n    grpo_vs_sft_standard_diff: -1.4\n    best_overall: SFT-Standard (63.5%)\n  result_rationale: 'N=1319会轻微调整N=100的点估计（regression to mean效应）。 SFT Standard的64%可能微降至63.5%，SFT\n    RASP的57%降至55.3%。 GRPO模型的full eval同样显示Standard优势持续。 关键发现：best recovered model是SFT-only\n    Standard（63.5%），不需要GRPO也不需要RASP。 这是worst档最damaging的result——最简单的pipeline（Standard\n    pruning + SFT）给出最好结果。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 4: Full Pipeline Comparison (N=1319)'\n    columns:\n    - Pipeline\n    - Post-Prune\n    - Post-Recovery\n    - Recovery Rate\n    rows:\n    - - RASP + SFT\n      - 29.3%\n      - 55.3%\n      - 55.4%\n    - - RASP + SFT→GRPO\n      - 29.3%\n      - 57.8%\n      - 60.7%\n    - - Standard + SFT\n      - 28.1%\n      - 63.5%\n      - 73.0%\n    - - Standard + SFT→GRPO\n      - 28.1%\n      - 62.1%\n      - 70.1%\n    - - Dense (no pruning)\n      - —\n      - 76.4%\n      - —\n    note: Recovery Rate = (post_recovery - post_prune) / (dense - post_prune)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: 4 pipelines的post-prune → post-SFT → post-GRPO三阶段accuracy'\n  - 'Recovery rate scatter: x=post-prune, y=recovery rate, 标注每个pipeline'\n  analysis: 'Paper Table 1的核心数据。Worst档的narrative：Standard+SFT是Pareto optimal—— 比所有其他pipeline更简单且更好。RASP的CKA-aware\n    pruning反而hurt了SFT recovery。 GRPO在两种pruning上的marginal/negative contribution质疑了RLVR\n    recovery的必要性 （至少在moderate sparsity下）。\n\n    '\n- name: GRASPrune Baseline 20%\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: GRASPrune（ACL 2026 SOTA）在20% sparsity下的完整pipeline：prune→eval→SFT→GRPO\n  expected_results:\n    grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.08\n    grasp_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.072\n    grasp_20_eos_rate: 0.02\n    grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_100: 0.58\n    grasp_20_post_sft_gsm8k_1319: 0.56\n    grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_100: 0.57\n    grasp_20_post_grpo_gsm8k_1319: 0.55\n    grasp_sft_recovery_gain_pp: 50\n    grasp_grpo_additional_gain_pp: -1\n  result_rationale: 'GRASPrune的post-prune accuracy极低（8%，已从grasp_baseline_westd观测到），\n    因为它优化的是budgeted pruning的immediate loss而非reasoning preservation。 但SFT recovery将其从8%拉到~58%（+50pp），这是worst档最重要的evidence之一：\n    post-prune accuracy与recovery outcome的correlation远低于预期。 GRASPrune post-prune最差（8%）但recovery后与RASP（57.8%）comparable。\n    这直接反驳了\"RASP preserves recoverable structures\"的claim—— 即使post-prune被摧毁到8%，SFT也能恢复到相似水平。\n    GRPO对GRASPrune同样无额外增益（-1pp regression）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 5: GRASPrune Pipeline Results'\n    columns:\n    - Stage\n    - Accuracy\n    - Gain from Previous\n    rows:\n    - - Post-Prune\n      - 7.2%\n      - -69.2pp from dense\n    - - Post-SFT\n      - 56.0%\n      - +48.8pp\n    - - Post-SFT→GRPO\n      - 55.0%\n      - -1.0pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Recovery trajectory plot: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard的三阶段accuracy变化，GRASPrune呈V形恢复'\n  analysis: 'GRASPrune的V形恢复是worst档的smoking gun：post-prune accuracy几乎不预测recovery outcome。\n    8%→56%的恢复意味着SFT的training signal足以重建大部分reasoning ability， regardless of which structures\n    were pruned。 这对所有recovery-aware pruning方法（包括RASP）都是existential challenge： 如果recovery主要由training\n    data驱动，优化pruning structure的marginal value极小。\n\n    '\n- name: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Eval (5 Seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 5个random seeds下RASP_20和Standard_20的post-prune GSM8K评估\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_20_seed42: 0.293\n    rasp_20_seed123: 0.285\n    rasp_20_seed456: 0.301\n    rasp_20_seed789: 0.278\n    rasp_20_seed1024: 0.289\n    rasp_20_mean: 0.289\n    rasp_20_std: 0.008\n    standard_20_seed42: 0.281\n    standard_20_seed123: 0.275\n    standard_20_seed456: 0.292\n    standard_20_seed789: 0.269\n    standard_20_seed1024: 0.283\n    standard_20_mean: 0.28\n    standard_20_std: 0.008\n    pairwise_gap_mean_pp: 0.9\n    pairwise_gap_std: 0.6\n    paired_t_test_p: 0.15\n    wilcoxon_p: 0.19\n    cohens_d: 0.35\n  result_rationale: '5-seed评估下，RASP和Standard的均值gap约0.9pp，标准差~0.8pp。 Paired t-test\n    p=0.15，Wilcoxon p=0.19——均不达显著性阈值（p<0.05）。 Cohen''s d=0.35属于small effect size。\n    seed-to-seed的方差（~0.8pp std）与gap本身（0.9pp）同量级， 说明观测到的gap完全可以被eval noise解释。 Worst档的关键：5-seed的power不足以detect\n    <1pp的真实差异， 但这恰恰说明即使存在真实差异也太小to be practically meaningful。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 6: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Results'\n    columns:\n    - Seed\n    - RASP-20\n    - Standard-20\n    - Δ\n    rows:\n    - - 42\n      - 29.3%\n      - 28.1%\n      - +1.2pp\n    - - 123\n      - 28.5%\n      - 27.5%\n      - +1.0pp\n    - - 456\n      - 30.1%\n      - 29.2%\n      - +0.9pp\n    - - 789\n      - 27.8%\n      - 26.9%\n      - +0.9pp\n    - - 1024\n      - 28.9%\n      - 28.3%\n      - +0.6pp\n    - - Mean±Std\n      - 28.9±0.8%\n      - 28.0±0.8%\n      - +0.9±0.6pp\n    - - p-value\n      - ''\n      - ''\n      - 0.15 (paired-t)\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Paired dot plot: 每个seed一条线连接RASP和Standard，几乎所有线都近乎水平'\n  - 'Box plot: RASP和Standard的5-seed分布高度重叠'\n  analysis: 'Post-prune gap在统计上不显著（p=0.15），effect size小（d=0.35）。 论文中应honest report这个null\n    result， 并argue这个negative finding本身有价值： 在moderate sparsity下CKA reranking不改变pruning\n    outcome。\n\n    '\n- name: Scoring Ablation at 20% Sparsity\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random pruning对比RASP/Standard\n  expected_results:\n    magnitude_only_gsm8k_100: 0.27\n    gradient_only_gsm8k_100: 0.26\n    random_pruning_gsm8k_100: 0.14\n    rasp_alpha4_gsm8k_100: 0.4\n    standard_alpha0_gsm8k_100: 0.28\n    rasp_alpha1_gsm8k_100: 0.3\n    magnitude_only_gsm8k_1319: 0.265\n    gradient_only_gsm8k_1319: 0.255\n    random_pruning_gsm8k_1319: 0.135\n  result_rationale: 'Random pruning大幅劣于所有structured方法（14% vs 26-40%），证明pruning order\n    matters。 Magnitude-only（27%）≈ Standard（28%）≈ Gradient-only（26%）， 三种importance-based方法在moderate\n    sparsity下几乎等价。 RASP α=4（40%）显著优于所有α=0方法——但这主要是α scaling的效果，不是CKA。 关键ablation：α=1（CKA权重较弱）只给30%，仅比Standard好2pp。\n    α=4的大幅提升（+12pp over Standard）更可能是importance distribution的reshaping效应 （α放大了high-overlap\n    groups的penalty，但也放大了importance的tail）， 而非CKA functional overlap的predictive value。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 7: Scoring Ablation (N=100, 20% Sparsity)'\n    columns:\n    - Scoring Method\n    - Post-Prune GSM8K\n    - vs Standard Δ\n    rows:\n    - - Random\n      - 14%\n      - -14pp\n    - - Gradient-only\n      - 26%\n      - -2pp\n    - - Magnitude-only\n      - 27%\n      - -1pp\n    - - Standard (Wanda I(h))\n      - 28%\n      - —\n    - - RASP α=1.0\n      - 30%\n      - +2pp\n    - - RASP α=4.0\n      - 40%\n      - +12pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: 6种scoring方法的post-prune accuracy，α=4.0是clear outlier'\n  - 'Decomposition plot: 将α=4.0的12pp gain分解为importance-scaling vs CKA-specific贡献'\n  analysis: 'α=4.0的优势（+12pp）是worst档的positive takeaway，但解释需要carefully nuanced。 α scaling本质上改变了importance\n    score的distribution shape—— 它upweight了already-important structures并downweight了marginal\n    ones， CKA项(1-F(h))只是这个rescaling的vehicle之一。 为证明这一点：可以test α-scaled magnitude-only（I(h)^α\n    without CKA）， 如果效果similar则CKA的独立贡献为零。 论文中应将此framed为\"α-scaled importance scoring\n    improves pruning\"而非\"CKA predicts recoverability\"。\n\n    '\n- name: CKA-Recoverability Correlation Analysis\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: Per-structure CKA F(h)与post-recovery accuracy retention的mixed-effects\n    regression\n  expected_results:\n    n_mlp_groups: 784\n    n_pruned_mlp_groups: 200\n    cka_beta_coefficient: 0.08\n    cka_beta_p_value: 0.12\n    cka_incremental_r2: 0.018\n    weight_norm_beta: 0.23\n    weight_norm_p: 0.001\n    gradient_importance_beta: 0.31\n    gradient_importance_p: 0.0003\n    activation_magnitude_beta: 0.19\n    activation_magnitude_p: 0.004\n    full_model_r2: 0.34\n    model_without_cka_r2: 0.32\n    layer_random_effect_variance: 0.15\n    cka_spearman_with_recoverability: 0.11\n    cka_spearman_p: 0.09\n  result_rationale: 'Mixed-effects regression显示CKA β=0.08 (p=0.12)，不达显著性。 Incremental\n    R²仅0.018（1.8%），远低于useful predictor的阈值（通常>5%）。 相比之下weight norm（β=0.23, p=0.001）和gradient\n    importance（β=0.31, p=0.0003） 都是stronger predictors。 CKA functional overlap与recoverability的Spearman\n    ρ=0.11（p=0.09），borderline但不显著。 核心问题：CKA measures inter-head functional similarity，\n    但RLVR recovery不是通过\"redistribute function across heads\"实现的—— RLVR更多是global optimization\n    of the loss landscape， individual head的functional overlap对global recovery的predictive\n    power有限。 Layer random effect variance (0.15)较大，说明per-layer差异比per-head CKA更重要。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 8: Mixed-Effects Regression Results (MLP Groups, N=784)'\n    columns:\n    - Predictor\n    - β\n    - SE\n    - p-value\n    - Incremental R²\n    rows:\n    - - Gradient Importance\n      - '0.31'\n      - '0.06'\n      - <0.001\n      - '0.14'\n    - - Weight Norm\n      - '0.23'\n      - '0.05'\n      - '0.001'\n      - '0.09'\n    - - Activation Magnitude\n      - '0.19'\n      - '0.05'\n      - '0.004'\n      - '0.06'\n    - - CKA Overlap F(h)\n      - '0.08'\n      - '0.05'\n      - '0.12'\n      - '0.018'\n    - - Full Model R²\n      - ''\n      - ''\n      - ''\n      - '0.34'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: F(h) vs per-head recoverability，大量scatter，弱correlation线'\n  - 'Coefficient plot: 4个predictor的β with 95% CI，CKA的CI跨零'\n  - 'Partial regression plot: 控制其他变量后CKA的residual effect'\n  analysis: '这是Claim 2的直接否定。CKA functional overlap不是recoverability的significant predictor。\n    Traditional importance metrics（gradient, weight norm）解释了大部分variance。 论文reframe：functional\n    overlap是一个intuitively appealing but empirically unsupported predictor of recovery\n    outcomes。 Positive spin：实验thoroughness（N=784, mixed-effects, covariates控制）使这个negative\n    result credible且publishable。\n\n    '\n- name: SFT-Only Recovery Comparison\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: Same pruned models, same data budget, SFT-only recovery（无GRPO）\n  expected_results:\n    sft_only_rasp_20_gsm8k_100: 0.57\n    sft_only_rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.553\n    sft_only_standard_20_gsm8k_100: 0.64\n    sft_only_standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.635\n    sft_only_gap_pp: -7\n    grpo_rasp_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.578\n    grpo_standard_20_gsm8k_1319: 0.621\n    interaction_f_test_p: 0.41\n    pruning_method_main_effect_p: 0.03\n    recovery_method_main_effect_p: 0.62\n    interaction_effect_size: 0.02\n  result_rationale: 'plan_002已完成SFT-only recovery（RASP 57%, Standard 64%）。 2×2 ANOVA\n    (pruning × recovery)显示： pruning method有main effect（Standard > RASP, p=0.03）， recovery\n    method无main effect（SFT ≈ SFT→GRPO, p=0.62）， 交互作用不显著（p=0.41）。 这意味着：Standard在两种recovery下都优于RASP，\n    且recovery method的选择不改变pruning方法的相对排名。 Claim 3（recovery method conditions optimal\n    pruning order）被直接否定。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 9: 2×2 Recovery Comparison (N=1319)'\n    columns:\n    - ''\n    - SFT-Only\n    - SFT→GRPO\n    - Δ(GRPO−SFT)\n    rows:\n    - - RASP-20\n      - 55.3%\n      - 57.8%\n      - +2.5pp\n    - - Standard-20\n      - 63.5%\n      - 62.1%\n      - -1.4pp\n    - - Δ(Std−RASP)\n      - +8.2pp\n      - +4.3pp\n      - ''\n  - name: 'Table 10: 2×2 ANOVA Results'\n    columns:\n    - Effect\n    - F\n    - p-value\n    - η²\n    rows:\n    - - Pruning Method\n      - '5.12'\n      - '0.03'\n      - '0.08'\n    - - Recovery Method\n      - '0.24'\n      - '0.62'\n      - '0.004'\n    - - Interaction\n      - '0.68'\n      - '0.41'\n      - '0.02'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Interaction plot: pruning method × recovery method，两条线近乎平行（无交互）'\n  analysis: 'Standard在两种recovery下一致优于RASP，GRPO不改变这个ranking。 Interaction plot的平行线直接visualize了null\n    interaction。 论文reframe为positive finding：SFT recovery is surprisingly robust——\n    无论pruning structure如何，SFT都能恢复到similar relative levels。 这暗示recovery robustness更多来自training\n    signal而非pruning structure。\n\n    '\n- name: 25% Sparsity RASP + Standard\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: 25% sparsity下完整pipeline：prune→eval→SFT→GRPO\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.18\n    rasp_25_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.172\n    standard_25_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.16\n    standard_25_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.155\n    postprune_gap_25_pp: 1.7\n    rasp_25_post_sft_100: 0.48\n    standard_25_post_sft_100: 0.52\n    rasp_25_post_grpo_100: 0.49\n    standard_25_post_grpo_100: 0.53\n    rasp_25_post_grpo_1319: 0.475\n    standard_25_post_grpo_1319: 0.515\n    recovery_rate_rasp_25: 0.512\n    recovery_rate_standard_25: 0.59\n  result_rationale: '25% sparsity下两种方法都受到更大损伤（17-18% post-prune vs 28-29% at 20%）。\n    RASP仍然略优于Standard在post-prune（+1.7pp），但gap依然不显著。 SFT recovery将两者提升到48-52%，Standard再次优于RASP。\n    GRPO在25% sparsity下同样无额外增益（+1pp for RASP, +1pp for Standard）。 关键观察：从20%到25%，recovery\n    ceiling从~63%降到~53%（-10pp）， 说明sparsity对recovery outcome的影响远大于pruning method的影响。\n    这进一步support了worst档的narrative：pruning structure的精细选择 相比sparsity ratio本身是second-order\n    effect。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 11: 25% Sparsity Pipeline'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Post-Prune\n    - Post-SFT\n    - Post-GRPO\n    rows:\n    - - RASP-25\n      - 17.2%\n      - 48%\n      - 49%\n    - - Standard-25\n      - 15.5%\n      - 52%\n      - 53%\n    - - Δ (RASP−Std)\n      - +1.7pp\n      - -4pp\n      - -4pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Sparsity × accuracy curve: 20% and 25%下RASP和Standard的recovery trajectories'\n  - 'Recovery ceiling plot: sparsity ratio vs best-recovered accuracy'\n  analysis: '25% sparsity数据确认20%的pattern scales：Standard consistently recovers better，\n    GRPO consistently unhelpful。Sparsity ratio是dominant factor。 论文中这作为robustness check，strengthen\n    negative findings的generality。\n\n    '\n- name: 30% Sparsity Probe\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: 30% sparsity下prune + eval only（无recovery），mapping collapse threshold\n  expected_results:\n    rasp_30_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.05\n    standard_30_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.04\n    rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.15\n    standard_30_eos_rate: 0.08\n    rasp_30_avg_len: 3200\n    standard_30_avg_len: 3800\n    gap_pp: 1\n  result_rationale: '30% sparsity下两种方法都near-collapse（5% vs 4%）， consistent with已知的35%\n    sparsity完全collapse（D005）。 RASP的marginal advantage缩小到1pp（在noise范围内）。 EOS rate大幅下降说明模型生成能力严重受损。\n    不做recovery是正确决策——从5%恢复的cost-benefit不合理。 这个data point完成了sparsity response curve：20%(29%)→25%(17%)→30%(5%)→35%(~0%)。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 12: 30% Sparsity Probe'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Post-Prune\n    - EOS Rate\n    - Avg Length\n    rows:\n    - - RASP-30\n      - 5%\n      - 15%\n      - '3200'\n    - - Standard-30\n      - 4%\n      - 8%\n      - '3800'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Sparsity response curve: 0-35% sparsity下的post-prune accuracy for RASP和Standard'\n  analysis: '30% sparsity是\"no man''s land\"——pruning too aggressive for meaningful\n    recovery。 两种方法无差异。curve shape（smooth degradation 20-25%, cliff 25-30%） suggests\n    a phase transition around 27-28% sparsity for this model。\n\n    '\n- name: OOD Evaluation (MATH-500, HumanEval)\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: Best recovered models在MATH-500和HumanEval上的OOD泛化评估\n  expected_results:\n    dense_math500: 0.52\n    dense_humaneval: 0.58\n    grpo_rasp_20_math500: 0.24\n    grpo_rasp_20_humaneval: 0.31\n    grpo_standard_20_math500: 0.28\n    grpo_standard_20_humaneval: 0.35\n    sft_standard_20_math500: 0.3\n    sft_standard_20_humaneval: 0.37\n    rasp_math500_advantage_pp: -4\n    rasp_humaneval_advantage_pp: -4\n    math500_recovery_rate_rasp: 0.36\n    math500_recovery_rate_standard: 0.46\n  result_rationale: 'OOD eval显示RASP在MATH-500和HumanEval上均劣于Standard（-4pp each）。 Standard的OOD优势与GSM8K上的优势consistent——\n    不是GSM8K-specific pattern memorization而是genuine reasoning recovery。 RASP的OOD劣势可能因为CKA-aware\n    pruning保留的structures 对GSM8K distribution更specific而非general reasoning structures。\n    所有recovered模型的OOD performance大幅低于dense baseline （MATH-500: 24-30% vs 52%），说明pruning+recovery的reasoning\n    preservation 对distribution shift很脆弱。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 13: OOD Evaluation'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - GSM8K\n    - MATH-500\n    - HumanEval\n    rows:\n    - - Dense Baseline\n      - 76.4%\n      - 52%\n      - 58%\n    - - RASP-20 + GRPO\n      - 57.8%\n      - 24%\n      - 31%\n    - - Standard-20 + GRPO\n      - 62.1%\n      - 28%\n      - 35%\n    - - Standard-20 + SFT\n      - 63.5%\n      - 30%\n      - 37%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Radar chart: 4个模型在3个benchmark上的coverage'\n  - 'Recovery rate by domain: GSM8K vs MATH-500 vs HumanEval的recovery rates对比'\n  analysis: 'OOD results消除了\"Standard SFT recovery只是memorization\"的concern—— Standard在所有domains上都consistently\n    better。 RASP在OOD上的劣势进一步weaken了recovery-aware pruning的motivation。 论文中：recovery后的OOD\n    degradation是under-explored area， 无论pruning方法如何，recovery都有significant OOD cost。\n\n    '\n- name: Bonsai Baseline 20%\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: Bonsai（ICML 2025 gradient-free structured pruning）在20%下的baseline\n  expected_results:\n    bonsai_20_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.25\n    bonsai_20_post_sft_100: 0.59\n    bonsai_20_post_grpo_100: 0.58\n    bonsai_vs_standard_postprune_pp: -3\n    bonsai_vs_standard_post_sft_pp: -5\n  result_rationale: 'Bonsai作为gradient-free方法在post-prune略低于Standard/RASP（25% vs 27-29%），\n    因为它不使用gradient信号。SFT recovery后达到59%， 与RASP（57%）comparable但低于Standard（64%）。 GRPO同样无额外增益。\n    Bonsai的表现pattern与RASP/Standard一致——SFT是primary recovery driver， pruning method间差异在recovery后收敛。\n    作为lower-priority baseline，主要价值是扩展method coverage。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 14: Bonsai Baseline'\n    columns:\n    - Stage\n    - Bonsai-20\n    - RASP-20\n    - Standard-20\n    rows:\n    - - Post-Prune\n      - 25%\n      - 29%\n      - 28%\n    - - Post-SFT\n      - 59%\n      - 57%\n      - 64%\n    - - Post-GRPO\n      - 58%\n      - 59%\n      - 63%\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Bonsai加入后method coverage达到4种（RASP, Standard, GRASPrune, Bonsai）。 Pattern一致：post-prune差异大，SFT\n    recovery后差异缩小，GRPO无额外贡献。 strengthen了\"recovery dominates pruning structure\"的narrative。\n\n    '\n- name: CKA Reliability Analysis\n  plan_id: plan_014\n  description: CKA scoring的split-half consistency和calibration size sensitivity\n  expected_results:\n    split_half_spearman_rho: 0.93\n    split_half_p_value: <0.0001\n    cal_256_vs_512_rank_correlation: 0.96\n    cal_512_vs_1024_rank_correlation: 0.98\n    cal_256_vs_1024_rank_correlation: 0.94\n    cka_score_cv_across_splits: 0.04\n  result_rationale: 'CKA scoring本身是highly reliable（ρ=0.93, consistent across calibration\n    sizes）。 这是一个important nuance：CKA作为measurement工具是可靠的， 问题不在于CKA的reliability而在于它measured\n    property（functional overlap） 与recoverability之间的relationship是weak的。 Split-half\n    ρ=0.93说明CKA scores不是noisy estimates—— 它们accurately capture了functional overlap，只是这个overlap不predicts\n    recovery。 Cal size sensitivity低（256→1024 rank correlation >0.94）说明256 samples足够。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 15: CKA Reliability'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Value\n    rows:\n    - - Split-half Spearman ρ\n      - '0.93'\n    - - Cal 256 vs 1024 rank ρ\n      - '0.94'\n    - - CKA score CV across splits\n      - '0.04'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Split-half scatter: two halves的CKA scores高度correlated'\n  analysis: 'CKA reliability高strengthens negative finding的credibility—— 不是因为measurement\n    noise导致CKA不predictive， 而是functional overlap genuinely不是recoverability的good predictor。\n    论文中这作为methodological rigor的evidence。\n\n    '\n- name: α Sensitivity Ablation\n  plan_id: plan_015\n  description: α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} sweep在RASP scoring S(h)=I(h)×(1-F(h))^α\n  expected_results:\n    alpha_0_gsm8k_100: 0.28\n    alpha_0p25_gsm8k_100: 0.28\n    alpha_0p5_gsm8k_100: 0.29\n    alpha_1p0_gsm8k_100: 0.3\n    alpha_2p0_gsm8k_100: 0.34\n    alpha_4p0_gsm8k_100: 0.4\n    alpha_optimal: 4.0\n    alpha_0_vs_optimal_gap_pp: 12\n    alpha_monotonic: true\n    alpha_1p0_sft_recovery: 0.59\n    alpha_4p0_sft_recovery: 0.62\n    alpha_0_sft_recovery: 0.64\n  result_rationale: 'α=0即Standard pruning（28%），α=4.0给出最优post-prune（40%，+12pp，已观测）。\n    Relationship monotonically increasing with α，suggesting α主要作为importance score的\n    exponential rescaling——higher α更aggressively保护high-importance structures。 但关键反转发生在SFT\n    recovery后：α=0（Standard）恢复到64%， α=4.0恢复到62%，α=1.0恢复到59%。 Post-prune advantage（α=4.0\n    > α=0 by 12pp）在SFT recovery后不仅消失还反转 （α=0 > α=4.0 by 2pp）。 这是worst档最subtle但重要的finding：α\n    scaling优化了wrong objective（post-prune accuracy） 而非最终目标（post-recovery accuracy）。\n    RASP的α scaling helps post-prune但hurts recovery—— 因为它over-protects structures that\n    are important but not SFT-recoverable， 同时under-removes structures that are less\n    important but carry SFT-friendly gradients。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 16: α Ablation Results'\n    columns:\n    - α\n    - Post-Prune GSM8K\n    - Post-SFT GSM8K\n    - Post-SFT→GRPO\n    rows:\n    - - 0 (Standard)\n      - 28%\n      - 64%\n      - 63%\n    - - '0.25'\n      - 28%\n      - 63%\n      - 62%\n    - - '0.5'\n      - 29%\n      - 62%\n      - 62%\n    - - '1.0'\n      - 30%\n      - 59%\n      - 60%\n    - - '2.0'\n      - 34%\n      - 60%\n      - 60%\n    - - '4.0'\n      - 40%\n      - 62%\n      - 59%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Dual-axis plot: α vs post-prune accuracy (ascending) 和 α vs post-recovery accuracy\n    (U-shaped/flat)'\n  - 'Pareto frontier: post-prune vs post-recovery accuracy across α values'\n  analysis: 'α ablation是worst档最nuanced的finding。 Post-prune: α scaling works（monotonic\n    improvement up to +12pp）。 Post-recovery: α scaling effect vanishes or reverses。\n    这creates an interesting decoupling：optimizing post-prune ≠ optimizing post-recovery。\n    论文positive takeaway：α scaling确实是effective pruning intervention， 但其mechanism是importance\n    distribution reshaping而非CKA-driven recoverability prediction。 Post-recovery的non-monotonic\n    pattern suggests α=0（no CKA weighting） 可能accidentally produce structures that\n    are more SFT-receptive。\n\n    '\n- name: Inference Speedup Benchmark\n  plan_id: plan_016\n  description: Dense vs RASP-20 vs Standard-20的wall-clock latency和throughput对比\n  expected_results:\n    dense_latency_ms_per_token: 28.5\n    rasp_20_latency_ms_per_token: 25.2\n    standard_20_latency_ms_per_token: 25.0\n    speedup_rasp_vs_dense: 1.13\n    speedup_standard_vs_dense: 1.14\n    dense_throughput_tokens_per_sec: 35.1\n    rasp_20_throughput: 39.7\n    standard_20_throughput: 40.0\n    memory_reduction_percent: 18.5\n    rasp_vs_standard_speedup_diff: <1%\n  result_rationale: 'Structured pruning at 20%理论上减少20% FLOPs， 但实际speedup仅~1.13x due\n    to hardware underutilization at small batch sizes 和memory bandwidth bottlenecks。\n    RASP和Standard的speedup几乎identical（1.13x vs 1.14x）因为两者prune相同数量的structures， 只是选择了不同的specific\n    structures。 Memory reduction (~18.5%)接近理论值，这是structured pruning的practical advantage。\n    Speedup ratio在[1.08, 1.18]范围内，符合worst档预期—— 不算impressive但足以demonstrate structured\n    pruning的practical motivation。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 17: Inference Speedup'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Latency (ms/tok)\n    - Throughput (tok/s)\n    - Memory (GB)\n    rows:\n    - - Dense\n      - '28.5'\n      - '35.1'\n      - '14.2'\n    - - RASP-20\n      - '25.2'\n      - '39.7'\n      - '11.6'\n    - - Standard-20\n      - '25.0'\n      - '40.0'\n      - '11.5'\n    - - Speedup vs Dense\n      - 1.13×/1.14×\n      - 1.13×/1.14×\n      - 18.3%/19.0% saved\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: latency comparison with error bars'\n  analysis: 'Speedup modest but real (1.13x)。两种pruning方法的efficiency完全相同。 这reinforces\n    worst档的point：pruning structure选择不影响practical outcomes （neither accuracy post-recovery\n    nor inference efficiency）。 论文中作为实用性baseline data。\n\n    '\n- name: Unstructured Pruning Baseline 20%\n  plan_id: plan_017\n  description: Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20%作为对比baseline\n  expected_results:\n    unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k_100: 0.56\n    unstructured_20_postprune_gsm8k_1319: 0.545\n    unstructured_20_post_sft_100: 0.64\n    unstructured_20_post_grpo_100: 0.65\n    unstructured_20_post_grpo_1319: 0.635\n    unstructured_vs_best_structured_pp: -0.5\n    unstructured_speedup_ratio: 1.02\n    unstructured_memory_saved: 0\n  result_rationale: 'Unstructured pruning at 20%保留了远多于structured pruning的post-prune\n    accuracy （56% vs 28-29%）因为它pruning individual weights而非entire channel groups。\n    SFT recovery仅marginal gain（56%→64%），因为post-prune already decent。 GRPO adds 1pp\n    to 65%。 但unstructured pruning几乎无speedup（1.02x）因为sparse tensors不efficiently map\n    to GPU hardware。 最终recovered accuracy（65%）与structured Standard+SFT（64%）comparable——\n    structured pruning通过recovery \"catches up\" to unstructured的保留能力。 这是一个interesting\n    finding for worst档： structured pruning + SFT recovery ≈ unstructured pruning in\n    accuracy， 但structured provides real speedup（1.13x vs 1.02x）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 18: Unstructured vs Structured Comparison'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Post-Prune\n    - Post-Recovery\n    - Speedup\n    rows:\n    - - Unstructured 20%\n      - 54.5%\n      - 63.5%\n      - 1.02×\n    - - RASP-20 (structured)\n      - 29.3%\n      - 57.8%\n      - 1.13×\n    - - Standard-20 (structured)\n      - 28.1%\n      - 63.5%\n      - 1.14×\n    - - GRASPrune-20 (structured)\n      - 7.2%\n      - 55.0%\n      - 1.13×\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Accuracy vs speedup scatter: unstructured在upper-left (high acc, low speedup)，structured在lower-right'\n  analysis: 'Unstructured vs structured comparison highlights the recovery gap： structured\n    pruning损伤severe但SFT几乎完全bridges这个gap。 Standard structured + SFT matches unstructured\n    accuracy while providing real speedup。 这进一步supports SFT recovery的power—— 它能overcome\n    27pp的post-prune deficit（unstructured 55% vs structured 28%） 到达相同的recovered accuracy。\n\n    '\n- name: SFT OOD Eval Contingency\n  plan_id: plan_018\n  description: SFT-recovered Standard模型在MATH-500和HumanEval上的OOD评估\n  expected_results:\n    sft_standard_20_math500: 0.3\n    sft_standard_20_humaneval: 0.37\n    sft_rasp_20_math500: 0.25\n    sft_rasp_20_humaneval: 0.31\n    dense_math500: 0.52\n    dense_humaneval: 0.58\n    standard_sft_math500_recovery_rate: 0.42\n    rasp_sft_math500_recovery_rate: 0.35\n    standard_vs_rasp_ood_gap_math500_pp: 5\n    standard_vs_rasp_ood_gap_humaneval_pp: 6\n  result_rationale: 'Standard的SFT recovery（1%→64% GSM8K jump——虽然在reeval后是28%→64%）\n    是否只是GSM8K pattern memorization？OOD eval显示NO： Standard在MATH-500（30%）和HumanEval（37%）上也consistently\n    outperform RASP（25%, 31%）。 Standard的OOD advantage（+5-6pp）甚至略大于in-distribution\n    advantage（+7pp GSM8K）， 说明Standard的SFT recovery建立了genuinely better reasoning ability而非memorization。\n    这是worst档对RASP最damaging的evidence之一—— 即使在OOD evaluation下RASP也consistently inferior。\n    Recovery后的OOD performance大幅低于dense baseline （MATH-500: 25-30% vs 52%），indicating\n    significant OOD fragility for all pruned models。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 19: SFT OOD Evaluation'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - GSM8K (ID)\n    - MATH-500 (OOD)\n    - HumanEval (OOD)\n    rows:\n    - - Dense\n      - 76.4%\n      - 52%\n      - 58%\n    - - Standard-20 + SFT\n      - 63.5%\n      - 30%\n      - 37%\n    - - RASP-20 + SFT\n      - 55.3%\n      - 25%\n      - 31%\n    - - Δ (Std−RASP)\n      - +8.2pp\n      - +5pp\n      - +6pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: ID vs OOD performance for SFT-recovered models'\n  analysis: OOD eval eliminates memorization concern。Standard的recovery advantage is\n    genuine。 论文中这应作为robustness evidence， framed as：Standard pruning + SFT produces\n    more generalizable recovery than RASP + SFT。 Implication：CKA-aware structure selection优化了wrong\n    representational properties， 可能保留了task-specific circuits而非general reasoning scaffolding。\n","numLines":974,"startLine":1,"totalLines":974}}}
