{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01D18WWVtvSHTgSDjYQYALBs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read both the PDF paper and the review context YAML. Let me analyze them carefully before dispatching the two reviewers.\n\nThe paper is \"Do Reasoning LLMs Need Recovery-Aware Pruning? A Controlled Empirical Study.\" It tests whether CKA-based functional overlap can guide structured pruning for better post-recovery performance in reasoning LLMs. The main findings are negative: CKA doesn't predict recoverability, Standard+SFT beats RASP+SFT, GRPO adds nothing over SFT.\n\nThe review context YAML provides the full imagined experiment list (18 experiments) with expected results. Let me check coverage:\n\n\nNow I'm going through the experiments listed in the context YAML and cross-referencing them with the tables in the paper. I can see the post-pruning evaluations, recovery results across different stages, multi-seed experiments, and ablation studies all accounted for in the paper's tables. Finishing up the experiment checklist with the remaining two items, then I'm ready to set up the reviewer panel—one focused on methods and experiments, the other on novelty and related work. I'll run them in parallel and then bring them together through a structured roundtable process.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40360,"cache_read_input_tokens":22962,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40360},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"338b77c3-ab77-4d20-989d-1a060abc37a8","uuid":"b81ad637-9a13-4792-85f8-affb5add32c6"}
