{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QiKtdScymzUkAP4FzV7Ytj","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/paper_provenance.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"paper:\\\\n  title: ''\\\\n  version: 8\\\\n  generated_at: '2026-05-15T07:15:37.156593+00:00'\\\\nclaims:\\\\n- id: C001\\\\n  location:\\\\n    section: experiments\\\\n    paragraph: 0\\\\n    sentence: 0\\\\n  text: CKA functional overlap predicts recoverability of pruned groups under RLVR\\\\n  type: empirical\\\\n  evidence:\\\\n  - 'mvp_rasp_pipeline: Spearman correlation between F(h) and per-group recoverability'\\\\n  decisions:\\\\n  - D001\\\\n  deprecated: false\\\\n- id: C003\\\\n  location:\\\\n    section: experiments\\\\n    paragraph: 0\\\\n    sentence: 0\\\\n  text: RASP achieves higher post-recovery accuracy than importance-only pruning at\\\\n    35% sparsity\\\\n  type: empirical\\\\n  evidence:\\\\n  - 'mvp_rasp_pipeline: GSM8K accuracy comparison Standard vs RASP after GRPO'\\\\n  decisions:\\\\n  - D001\\\\n  deprecated: false\\\\n- id: C006\\\\n  location:\\\\n    section: experiments\\\\n    paragraph: 0\\\\n    sentence: 0\\\\n  text: At 35% sparsity, global importance ranking naturally prunes only MLP groups\\\\n  type: empirical\\\\n  evidence:\\\\n  - 'mvp_rasp_pipeline: pruning mask analysis showing attention groups retained'\\\\n  decisions:\\\\n  - D001\\\\n  deprecated: false\\\\n- id: C007\\\\n  location:\\\\n    section: method\\\\n    paragraph: 0\\\\n    sentence: 0\\\\n  text: RASP scoring S(h) = I(h) × (1-F(h))^α protects functionally unique structures\\\\n    while allowing removal of high-overlap structures recoverable via RLVR\\\\n  type: methodological\\\\n  evidence:\\\\n  - eq:score definition\\\\n  - rlsqueezes2026 theoretical basis\\\\n  decisions: []\\\\n  deprecated: false\\\\n- id: C009\\\\n  location:\\\\n    section: method\\\\n    paragraph: 0\\\\n    sentence: 0\\\\n  text: Per-layer capacity floor (≥40% MLP groups) prevents representational collapse\\\\n    from unconstrained global ranking\\\\n  type: methodological\\\\n  evidence:\\\\n  - observed failure at 20% sparsity without floor (mvp_rasp_pipeline_v2/v3)\\\\n  decisions: []\\\\n  deprecated: false\\\\n- id: C012\\\\n  location:\\\\n    section: method\\\\n    paragraph: 0\\\\n    sentence: 0\\\\n  text: Two-stage recovery (SFT warmup → GRPO) is necessary because direct GRPO fails\\\\n    on pruned models due to EOS collapse\\\\n  type: methodological\\\\n  evidence:\\\\n  - 'grpo_rasp_20_4096: clipped_ratio=1.0, grad_norm=0'\\\\n  - 'grpo_standard_20_4096: same failure'\\\\n  decisions: []\\\\n  deprecated: false\\\\n- id: C013\\\\n  location:\\\\n    section: related_work\\\\n    paragraph: 0\\\\n    sentence: 0\\\\n  text: No prior work optimizes pruning decisions for post-RLVR recoverability\\\\n  type: positioning\\\\n  evidence:\\\\n  - survey of 15+ pruning/recovery papers\\\\n  decisions: []\\\\n  deprecated: false\\\\n- id: C015\\\\n  location:\\\\n    section: related_work\\\\n    paragraph: 0\\\\n    sentence: 0\\\\n  text: 'RASP extends LTH to paradigm-conditioned trainability: optimal subnetwork\\\\n    depends on recovery paradigm'\\\\n  type: conceptual\\\\n  evidence:\\\\n  - frankle2019lth\\\\n  - rlsqueezes2026\\\\n  decisions: []\\\\n  deprecated: false\\\\n- id: C018\\\\n  location:\\\\n    section: related_work\\\\n    paragraph: 0\\\\n    sentence: 0\\\\n  text: RASP uses intra-layer CKA (width pruning) vs prior work inter-layer CKA (depth\\\\n    pruning) — different granularity and objective\\\\n  type: positioning\\\\n  evidence:\\\\n  - mpruner2024\\\\n  - lachance2024cka\\\\n  - kornblith2019cka\\\\n  decisions: []\\\\n  deprecated: false\\\\n- id: C019\\\\n  location:\\\\n    section: introduction\\\\n    paragraph: 0\\\\n    sentence: 0\\\\n  text: 'Redund